  len (line 1): a scan for the terminating zero: n += strlen(s + n)
    proof: structural (C99 7.21.6.3: strlen counts the characters before the first null; the loop steps over exactly those, reading the same bytes (a signed counter past its maximum is UB)); cost: a byte loop -> the C library's strlen
    before: while(s[n])n++;
    after:  n += strlen((const char *)s + n);
  lenp (line 2): a scan for the terminating zero: p += strlen(p)
    proof: structural (C99 7.21.6.3: strlen counts the characters before the first null; the loop steps over exactly those, reading the same bytes); cost: a byte loop -> the C library's strlen
    before: while(*p)p++;
    after:  p += strlen((const char *)p);
