  lenp (line 2): not lowered: line 2: a parameter that is not an integer or a float (s)
optimised C:
  /* optimised by ucas cfront for x86-64-v3 (x86-64-v3); every rewrite proved, see the report */
  #include <stdint.h>
  #include <string.h>
  int len(const char*s){int n=0;n += strlen((const char *)s + n);return n;}
  int lenp(const char*s){const char*p=s;p += strlen((const char *)p);return p-s;}
